<% content_for :title, "Progress" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Components</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Progress</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A determinate progress bar. Renders <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role="progressbar"</code>
    with <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-valuenow</code>/<code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-valuemax</code>
    and a required accessible name.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="progress-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted grid gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Uploading photo.png — 60%</p>
    <%= render Ui::ProgressComponent.new(value: 60, label: "Uploading photo.png") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Step 3 of 5</p>
    <%= render Ui::ProgressComponent.new(value: 3, max: 5, label: "Step 3 of 5") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Waiting to start — 0%</p>
    <%= render Ui::ProgressComponent.new(label: "Waiting to start") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Complete — 100%</p>
    <%= render Ui::ProgressComponent.new(value: 100, label: "Import complete") %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <h3 id="disk-usage-heading" class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Disk usage — 82%</h3>
    <%= render Ui::ProgressComponent.new(value: 82, aria: { labelledby: "disk-usage-heading" }) %>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-2">
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Storage nearly full — 90%</p>
    <%= render Ui::ProgressComponent.new(value: 90, label: "Storage nearly full", class: "bg-destructive/20") %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#progress-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="progress-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_progress_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["value", "Numeric", "nil",  "The current value, clamped to 0..max. nil renders as 0 -- always a real number, never indeterminate."],
        ["max",   "Numeric", "100",  "The value the bar is complete at. Drives aria-valuemax and the fill's percentage."],
        ["label", "String",  "nil",  "The accessible name, rendered as aria-label. Required unless you forward your own aria: { label: }/{ labelledby: }; missing both raises in development and test."],
        ["class", "String",  "nil",  "Merged over the default classes with tailwind_merge -- recolours the track. The fill stays on bg-primary, the token that carries the meaning."],
        ["…",     "Any",     "—",    "Every other keyword (id:, data:, …) is forwarded to the root element."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Notes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>Renders a <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;div role="progressbar"&gt;</code>, not the native <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;progress&gt;</code> element. Native <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;progress&gt;</code> was tried first, but its track and fill are only reachable through non-standard vendor pseudo-elements that paint correctly yet return nothing to a colour probe -- there's no real DOM node to verify the fill reaches 3:1 against the track. This is also what shadcn/ui itself ships for Progress.</li>
  <li>Determinate only -- there's no indeterminate state. A missing <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">value:</code> renders at 0 rather than leaving the bar without one.</li>
  <li>The accessible name is required. A percentage with no name announced doesn't tell anyone what's progressing, so pass <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">label:</code> or point <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria-labelledby</code> at a visible heading yourself.</li>
  <li>No Stimulus controller. Re-render with a new <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">value:</code> from your own state -- a Turbo Stream, a poll, an upload progress event.</li>
</ul>
